 else needs to take over his or her work schedule for the vacation period.</LongDescription><sap:tagcollection><sap:tag>Employee Central (EC)</sap:tag><sap:tag>EC - Time Off</sap:tag></sap:tagcollection></Documentation></EntitySet><EntitySet Name="DGFilter" EntityType="SFOData.DGFilter" sap:label="Dynamic Group Filter" sap:creatable="false" sap:updatable="false" sap:upsertable="false" sap:deletable="false"><Documentation><Summary>DGFilter</Summary><LongDescription>This entity represents filters for a given people pool.</LongDescription><sap:tagcollection><sap:tag>Foundation/Platform (PLT)</sap:tag><sap:tag>PLT - Role Based Permissions</sap:tag><sap:tag>Results List Not Supported</sap:tag></sap:tagcollection></Documentation></EntitySet><EntitySet Name="WfRequestStep" EntityType="SFOData.WfRequestStep" sap:label="WfRequestStep" sap:creatable="false" sap:updatable="false" sap:upsertable="false" sap:deletable="false"><Documentation><Summary>WfRequestStep</Summary><LongDescription>Contains information about a specific workflow step.</LongDescription><sap:tagcollection><sap:tag>Employee Central (EC)</sap:tag><sap:tag>EC - Workflow</sap:tag></sap:tagcollection></Documentation></EntitySet><EntitySet Name="PayScaleLevel" EntityType="SFOData.PayScaleLevel" sap:label="Pay Scale Level" sap:creatable="true" sap:updatable="true" sap:upsertable="true" sap:deletable="true"><Documentation><Summary></Summary><LongDescription>Contains information about pay scale level. Pay scale levels are subdivisions of pay scale groups. They often refer to the 'notch' that the employee is on within his pay scale group. They can also refer to the percentile in which the employee's salary falls into.</LongDescription><sap:tagcollection><sap:tag>Employee Central (EC)</sap:tag><sap:tag>EC - Foundation/Organization</sap:tag></sap:tagcollection></Documentation></EntitySet><EntitySet Name="TimeCollector" EntityType="SFOData.TimeCollector" sap:label="Time Collector" sap:creatable="false" sap:updatable="fal